{"kind":"request","text":"Implement kernel key rotation, the one reserved event type the kernel claims.","body":{"conditions":"The design gives the kernel exactly one reserved event type — a rotation envelope signed by the current sequencer key naming its successor — and the spike verifies every commit against the genesis key alone (spike/internal/kernel/kernel.go, scanHead), so sequencer key compromise or loss has no in-band remedy short of continuation. Add the rotation envelope; make verification walk the spine tracking the current key across rotations; refuse events signed by a retired key after its rotation point; test rotation mid-log, at head, and a forged rotation signed by a non-current key; state in docs/reference.md what rotation does and does not recover. Obtain independent exact-head review before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}